  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This 2025 dataset has a modest but already documented reuse record: seven downstream associated articles have been linked to it, showing that the underlying data and methods are being carried forward in related research. The record also identifies clear stewardship links to companion datasets and software, which helps situate this work within a broader reusable research workflow.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This dataset accompanies research on one-dimensional edge-localized Yu-Shiba-Rusinov states in CrCl\u2083 on NbSe\u2082, a condensed-matter physics study of a ferromagnet/superconductor heterostructure. The abstract indicates that low-temperature scanning tunneling microscopy was used to observe topologically trivial YSR states at the edges of CrCl\u2083 islands, and that density-functional-theory simulations were used to interpret the electronic structure at those edges.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest evidence of impact in the current record is reuse: seven downstream associated articles are linked to this dataset. That pattern suggests the resource is being incorporated into related scholarship, even though the article-level citation count remains at zero at this stage. In other words, the dataset is already part of a visible research chain, but formal citation accumulation has not yet begun to register.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The stewardship record is also informative. The dataset is connected to a companion DataCite dataset and to several software and article identifiers, indicating that it sits within a well-documented computational and experimental ecosystem rather than as a standalone archive. For a physics dataset of this kind, those relationships are an important sign of reproducibility and reuse potential.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Direct attention signals are otherwise sparse: the available record shows no DataCite views or downloads, no scite citation activity, and no documented public discourse in the indexed sources. That does not diminish the dataset\u2019s scholarly relevance; it simply means the measurable footprint is currently concentrated in downstream reuse and in the supporting infrastructure around the work.</p>",
